Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests Utilities list;
register(JitLadder);
define
    scL;
    scR;
    scA;
    scB;
    scN;
    scId code={ scN += 1; return argument; };
    scDriver code={
        scH := scId;
        scA = scL && *scH(scR);
        scB = *scH(scL) || scR;
        };
    ;
scL = 1; scR = 1; scN = 0;
testing(scDriver);
cerr "JSC jitted      calls " scN " a " scA " b " scB:;
scL = 1; scR = 1; scN = 0;
scDriver();
cerr "JSC interpreted calls " scN " a " scA " b " scB:;
cerr "JITSCCOUNT SENTINEL":;
stop();

jitScCountT -- SEQ 372 R2 (Tony, 2026-10-16): jitXscRT's shape with a call counter. Each AND/OR operand the jit
cannot emit (a starred call) runs at run time on the interpreted road (jitScOperandRT). A statement is handed over
ONCE: the boundary must not also hand the whole statement to jitStmtRT, or each call runs twice. The jitted count
must equal the interpreted count. scN is declared because two actions touch it (bear-trap #39).
